44 17592186045443 true] [17592186524174 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524160 13194139535644 17592186045443 true] [17592186524174 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535644 17592186045443 true] [17592186524174 1071 "What is the gradient of the product $f(x,y)h(x,y)$ if $f(x,y)=(x-3){e}^{(y+4)}$ and $h(x,y)=(y+4){e}^{(x-3)}?$" 13194139535644 17592186045443 true] [17592186524174 1072 #uuid "a18b5f63-dc6e-5c60-bea1-6d3675dd37d9" 13194139535644 17592186045443 true] [17592186524174 1074 "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[fh]=f\\,∇\\,h+h\\,∇\\,f\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-3){e}^{(y+4)})={e}^{(y+4)} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-3){e}^{(y+4)})=(x-3){e}^{(y+4)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\text{ }j={e}^{(y+4)}\\text{ }i+(x-3){e}^{(y+4)}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the partial derivatives of $h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((y+4){e}^{(x-3)})=(y+4){e}^{(x-3)} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((y+4){e}^{(x-3)})={e}^{(x-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y) & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\text{ }j=(y+4){e}^{(x-3)}\\text{ }i+{e}^{(x-3)}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the product rule, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)h(x,y)] & =(x-3){e}^{(y+4)}((y+4){e}^{(x-3)}\\text{ }i+{e}^{(x-3)}\\text{ }j)+(y+4){e}^{(x-3)}({e}^{(y+4)}\\text{ }i+(x-3){e}^{(y+4)}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(x-3)(y+4){e}^{(x-3)+(y+4)}\\text{ }i+(x-3){e}^{(x-3)+(y+4)}\\text{ }j+(y+4){e}^{(x-3)+(y+4)}\\text{ }i+(x-3)(y+4){e}^{(x-3)+(y+4)}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =((x-3)+1)(y+4){e}^{(x-3)+(y+4)}\\text{ }i+(x-3)(1+(y+4)){e}^{(x-3)+(y+4)}\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535644 17592186045443 true] [17592186524175 1080 "(32 x + 4 y)\\,i+(4 x - 12 y)\\,j" 13194139535644 175921